# Test: ze config validate ACCEPTS an mcp server entry that names no port
# VALIDATES: the operator-visible half of the port default. ze-mcp-conf.yang
# declares `refine port { default 8080; }` for environment/mcp/server, the Ze
# YANG compiler drops refine defaults, and extractMCPBlock
# (internal/component/config/loader_extract.go) now applies the same 8080 the
# schema promises. So the operator who reads the YANG and omits the port gets a
# listener on 127.0.0.1:8080, and validation says the config is valid.
# PREVENTS: the divergence returning -- a schema that promises a port the daemon
# ignores, and a config refused for following the document it was written from.
#
# Owner ruling 2026-08-23: the daemon applies the default, rather than the YANG
# dropping it, so mcp agrees with environment.web, environment.gnmi and
# environment.api-server. This file asserted the opposite until that ruling.
#
# Sibling: mcp-multi-listener.ci proves two entries that spell out their ports
# are accepted, and mcp-listener-port-default-disabled.ci proves a switched-off
# block starts nothing whatever its entries say.
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	router-id 10.0.0.1;
	session { asn { local 65533; } }
}
environment {
	mcp {
		enabled true;
		server primary {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid
